- **Progress (Reader-Preference)**:  
  Readers wait on `can_read` only when a writer is active. Writers wait on `can_write` only when readers are active. Since readers are allowed to proceed when no writer is active, and writers are blocked until all readers finish, the reader-preference rule is satisfied. No reader is starved — if a reader arrives, it will eventually proceed as long as no writer is active.

